{"name":"Longfellow","hex":"#90b1a3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Longfellow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname transferred from the nickname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Longfellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Henry Wadsworth Longfellow","blocks":[{"text":"Henry Wadsworth Longfellow was an American poet and educator. His original works include the poems \"Paul Revere's Ride\", The Song of Hiawatha, and Evangeline. He was the first American to completely translate Dante Alighieri's Divine Comedy and was one of the fireside poets from New England."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Henry_Wadsworth_Longfellow%2C_photographed_by_Julia_Margaret_Cameron_in_1868.jpg/330px-Henry_Wadsworth_Longfellow%2C_photographed_by_Julia_Margaret_Cameron_in_1868.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Wadsworth_Longfellow","wikidata":"Q152513"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Longfellow%27s_Birthplace%2C_Portland%2C_ME.jpg/500px-Longfellow%27s_Birthplace%2C_Portland%2C_ME.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Longfellow%27s_Birthplace%2C_Portland%2C_ME.jpg/500px-Longfellow%27s_Birthplace%2C_Portland%2C_ME.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Birthplace of Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, Portland, Maine, c. 1910; the house was demolished in 1955.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALongfellow's_Birthplace%2C_Portland%2C_ME.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Mary_Storer_Potter.JPG/250px-Mary_Storer_Potter.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/Mary_Storer_Potter.JPG?utm_source=en.wi